  'cn-num-crc-10011101': {
    blocks: ["Generator x³ + 1 = **1001** (degree 3), so append **3 zeros** and divide using XOR (mod-2) division.", {"code": "10011101000\n1001\n----\n00001101000\n    1001\n    ----\n    0100000\n     1001\n     ----\n     000100\nRemainder = 100"}, "Remainder = **100**. Transmitted frame = message + remainder = **10011101100**.", "**Error check:** inverting the 3rd bit from the left gives **10111101100**. Dividing it by 1001 leaves remainder **100** (not 000), so the receiver knows the frame is damaged.", {"tip": "At the receiver, divide the whole received frame by the same generator: remainder 0 means no error detected."}],
    sources: [U, `${TB} §3.2`],
  },

